<h1 id=3D"OmniOut(SharpenDB)-Introduction"><strong>Introduction</strong></h=
1>
<p>OmniOut is a solution for creating outbound dialing campaigns that can b=
e used by your agents, or alternatively, using Logic+ for automated outboun=
d calls, text, or email messaging. Before we begin, you will need to unders=
tand some vocabulary pertaining to OmniOut.</p>
<p><strong>OmniOut </strong>=E2=80=93 The outbound cadence tool.</p>
<p><strong>Campaign </strong>=E2=80=93 The container for the cadence stages=
. Also the mechanism by which outbound interactions are delivered to a queu=
e for handling.</p>
<p><strong>Cadence </strong>=E2=80=93 The order of activities in a campaign=
.</p>
<p><strong>Preview Dialing </strong>=E2=80=93 A type of step in the campaig=
n cadence where interactions are queued up for agents to answer and then pl=
ace a call, text, or email out to a lead.</p>
<p><strong>Agentless</strong> =E2=80=93 A type of step in the campaign cade=
nce in order to send SMS, Email, or Calls-to-IVR without agent intervention=
.</p>
<p><strong>Q Classifications</strong> =E2=80=93 Used to identify the result=
 of an interaction. Synonymous with =E2=80=98End Result=E2=80=99, =E2=80=98=
End Type=E2=80=99, and =E2=80=98Disposition=E2=80=99.</p>
<p><strong>Queues </strong>=E2=80=93 Identifies where outbound interaction =
will be handled by agents.</p>
