<p>This will pop up the Add Data Record. In the =E2=80=9CCampaign=E2=80=9D =
field, input the key that you copied from the previous step. You will need =
to determine the name of the campaign status and input it in the =E2=80=9CC=
ampaign Status Name=E2=80=9D field. Once you are complete, click =E2=80=9CC=
reate Record=E2=80=9D. To add another, select the =E2=80=9CAdd Another=E2=
=80=9D toggle. For most use cases, you will be creating additional statuses=
.</p><span class=3D"confluence-embedded-file-wrapper image-center-wrapper c=
onfluence-embedded-manual-size"><img class=3D"confluence-embedded-image ima=
ge-center" alt=3D"image-20250220-232509.png" width=3D"468" loading=3D"lazy"=
 src=3D"e4d62fadc55c05296def5dfcd1d04a78ef4c1e7356f76ce7fd2b8bd4c4ec0008" d=
ata-image-src=3D"https://sharpencx.atlassian.net/wiki/download/attachments/=
4509466637/image-20250220-232509.png?version=3D1&amp;modificationDate=3D174=
0093909679&amp;cacheVersion=3D1&amp;api=3Dv2" data-height=3D"458" data-widt=
h=3D"1287" data-unresolved-comment-count=3D"0" data-linked-resource-id=3D"4=
510646274" data-linked-resource-version=3D"1" data-linked-resource-type=3D"=
attachment" data-linked-resource-default-alias=3D"image-20250220-232509.png=
" data-base-url=3D"https://sharpencx.atlassian.net/wiki" data-linked-resour=
ce-content-type=3D"image/png" data-linked-resource-container-id=3D"45094666=
37" data-linked-resource-container-version=3D"12" data-media-id=3D"7bc85f23=
-2850-45d3-b1fa-dedfdaadd929" data-media-type=3D"file" height=3D"166"></spa=
n>
<p>For this example, we will be using the following campaign statuses:</p>
<p>Initial Call</p>
<p>Interested</p>
<p>Not Interested</p>
<p>Follow Up</p>
<p>No Answer</p>
<p>Do Not Call</p>
<p><strong>Tip: </strong>Ensure that there are no spaces before or after th=
e campaign key. A common mistake is leaving a space, which will cause your =
campaign statuses to not show up properly. If you have completed a campaign=
 and all appears to be configured correctly but it still fails to work, dou=
ble check for errant spaces.</p>
<h1 id=3D"OmniOut(SharpenDB)-ConfiguringQClassifications"><strong>Configuri=
ng Q Classifications</strong></h1>
<p>You will need to create Q Classifications to match each of the campaign =
statuses. Agents must select an end result at the conclusion of each intera=
ction because the OmniOut cadence is driven by the the result of the previo=
us interaction. This is completed under the Queue Classifications under the=
 Admin Configuration Menu.</p><span class=3D"confluence-embedded-file-wrapp=
er image-center-wrapper confluence-embedded-manual-size"><img class=3D"conf=
luence-embedded-image image-center" alt=3D"image-20250220-232545.png" width=
=3D"468" loading=3D"lazy" src=3D"4e6cdf4ac2588dee4bb94d65e92a95e8435540a0b6=
cc1eb5c85696be9a9d4354" data-image-src=3D"https://sharpencx.atlassian.net/w=
iki/download/attachments/4509466637/image-20250220-232545.png?version=3D1&a=
mp;modificationDate=3D1740093946059&amp;cacheVersion=3D1&amp;api=3Dv2" data=
-height=3D"592" data-width=3D"1279" data-unresolved-comment-count=3D"0" dat=
a-linked-resource-id=3D"4510744577" data-linked-resource-version=3D"1" data=
-linked-resource-type=3D"attachment" data-linked-resource-default-alias=3D"=
image-20250220-232545.png" data-base-url=3D"https://sharpencx.atlassian.net=
/wiki" data-linked-resource-content-type=3D"image/png" data-linked-resource=
-container-id=3D"4509466637" data-linked-resource-container-version=3D"12" =
data-media-id=3D"fa41a540-e9e5-4d9b-a149-e24881424908" data-media-type=3D"f=
ile" height=3D"216"></span>
<p>Once in the Q Classifications section of the admin application, click =
=E2=80=9CNew Classification=E2=80=9D</p><span class=3D"confluence-embedded-=
file-wrapper image-center-wrapper confluence-embedded-manual-size"><img cla=
ss=3D"confluence-embedded-image image-center" alt=3D"image-20250220-232628.=
png" width=3D"468" loading=3D"lazy" src=3D"a892196850ba8330a2248d48f82eb6a7=
c26b3b42f376c4ad8d747791d5636acd" data-image-src=3D"https://sharpencx.atlas=
sian.net/wiki/download/attachments/4509466637/image-20250220-232628.png?ver=
sion=3D1&amp;modificationDate=3D1740093989432&amp;cacheVersion=3D1&amp;api=
=3Dv2" data-height=3D"430" data-width=3D"1264" data-unresolved-comment-coun=
t=3D"0" data-linked-resource-id=3D"4510580740" data-linked-resource-version=
=3D"1" data-linked-resource-type=3D"attachment" data-linked-resource-defaul=
t-alias=3D"image-20250220-232628.png" data-base-url=3D"https://sharpencx.at=
lassian.net/wiki" data-linked-resource-content-type=3D"image/png" data-link=
ed-resource-container-id=3D"4509466637" data-linked-resource-container-vers=
ion=3D"12" data-media-id=3D"27bd4be3-14d2-49ce-80be-2c89ad542d4e" data-medi=
a-type=3D"file" height=3D"159"></span>
<p>Enter the name of the queue classification in the =E2=80=9CClassificatio=
n=E2=80=9D field. Select the queue that the queue classification should bel=
ong to in the =E2=80=9CLocation=E2=80=9D field. If the queue classification=
 should apply to all queues, select Global from the dropdown list. Once thi=
s is completed, Select =E2=80=9CEnd=E2=80=9D as the type, and then =E2=80=
=9CSave=E2=80=9D. There is an option to set a queue classification as =E2=
=80=9CDefault=E2=80=9D. This will set the end result of the call to the sel=
ected default queue classification if the agent fails to select one themsel=
ves.</p><span class=3D"confluence-embedded-file-wrapper image-center-wrappe=
r confluence-embedded-manual-size"><img class=3D"confluence-embedded-image =
image-center" alt=3D"image-20250220-232723.png" width=3D"468" loading=3D"la=
zy" src=3D"e67f2eb5b0e236a61cd4d840286689e91bb43d39915eada1ca1512e4b9238806=
" data-image-src=3D"https://sharpencx.atlassian.net/wiki/download/attachmen=
ts/4509466637/image-20250220-232723.png?version=3D1&amp;modificationDate=3D=
1740094043841&amp;cacheVersion=3D1&amp;api=3Dv2" data-height=3D"597" data-w=
idth=3D"1279" data-unresolved-comment-count=3D"0" data-linked-resource-id=
