<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>&nbsp;</p></td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>status*</p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>Varchar</p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>This is the stage in the campaign where you=E2=80=99d like to insert thi=
s contact (generally, you want the contact to go to the first stage of the =
campaign =E2=80=94 this gives you the option to leapfrog portions of the ca=
mpaign if necessary).</p></td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>owner*</p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>Varchar</p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>This is the particular owner you want to assign to the contact (e.g. if =
you want to handle Adam=E2=80=99s contacts differently from Ric=E2=80=99s, =
you=E2=80=99d enter the respective owner here).</p>
<p>If you don=E2=80=99t have a specific owner, insert an asterisk and the i=
nteractions will go to the default Q.</p></td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>imported*</p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>Tinyint</p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>This is a boolean field that lets OmniOut know whether a contact has bee=
n imported for a given stage yet.</p>
<p>Enter 0 (that=E2=80=99s a zero) for new contacts. This will change to 1 =
after the contact has been imported for a stage. Then, switch back to 0 whe=
n it transitions to the next stage.</p></td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>lastActionTime*</p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>Datetime</p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>This date/time field will populate with the last OmniOut import timestam=
p</p></td>
</tr>
</tbody>
</table>
</div>
