<div class=3D"table-wrap">
<table data-local-id=3D"517a6d66-e9ab-47d1-9e30-13845303d3a1" data-layout=
=3D"default" data-table-width=3D"760" class=3D"confluenceTable">
<tbody>
<tr>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p><strong>Queue</strong></p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>All available queues will display within this drop down. Ensure that you=
 select the appropriate outbound queue for this agent and the campaign you =
are configuring.</p>
<p>&nbsp;</p></td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p><strong>Calling Method</strong></p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>This determines how you=E2=80=99d like agents to proceed through the cam=
paign.</p>
<p><strong>Manual =E2=80=94 </strong>this is the most common option. This m=
eans the agent will be able to read any pertinent information about the cal=
l, the click the =E2=80=9CPlace Call=E2=80=9D button</p>
<p><strong>Automatic =E2=80=94 </strong>indicates that when an agent clicks=
 the =E2=80=9CAccept=E2=80=9D button, the call will be automatically placed=
. (There is no time to read about the call before dialing).</p></td>
</tr>
</tbody>
</table>
</div>
<p><strong>Tip: </strong>Omniout cannot be used with MyQs. You will need to=
 have a Sharpen Q Configured for agents to use that is accessible by the ag=
ents you would like to receive calls.</p>
<p><strong>Agentless Processing: </strong>You can send 250 items from Omnio=
ut to Logic+ every 5mins. Logic+ will process those 250 items at a rate of =
1 every 2 seconds.</p>
    </div>
</body>
